<pending_commit branch="chromeos-2015.07" change_id="I6c6bdce7e06712bc06cc620a3d7a6a6250c59c95" commit="84662296a63801950ecb0f2c0bcba1302162c3f9" commit_message="chromeos/vboot: provide support for x86 memory init verification  For x86 systems which resume through the reset vector one needs to ensure the the RW slot taken at resume time matches the one at boot time. The reason is that any assets pulled out of the boot media need to match how the platform previously booted. To do that one needs obtain the hash digest of the chosen slot, and it needs to be saved in a secure place on the normal boot path. On resume one needs to retrieve the hash digest back to compare it with the chosen slot. If they don't match resuming won't be possible.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:46049 BRANCH=glados TEST=Suspended and resumed on chell. Also, tested with an EC build      which returns a bad hash to ensure that is properly caught. CQ-DEPEND=CL:323460  Change-Id: I6c6bdce7e06712bc06cc620a3d7a6a6250c59c95 Signed-off-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/323500 Reviewed-by: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Duncan Laurie &lt;dlaurie@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="323500" owner_email="adurbin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/00/323500/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2015.07" change_id="I97318cec34494a7fc4b1ecf2cb22715d20e730ff" commit="06b2c158fb191f9d2054fa99c22cc29131359915" commit_message="chromeos/vboot: allow platform to hook into vboot_reboot()  Sometimes it's necessary for the platform to perform clean up tasks prior to reboot when employing vboot. For example, x86 systems that resume and do vboot verification may need to clear their sleep control register prior to doing a cold reset so that the next boot doesn't appear to be a resume. Allow that hook by introducing vboot_platform_prepare_reboot().  BUG=chrome-os-partner:46049 BRANCH=glados TEST=Ensure vboot_platform_prepare_reboot() called from vboot_reboot().  Change-Id: I97318cec34494a7fc4b1ecf2cb22715d20e730ff Signed-off-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/323501 Reviewed-by: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Duncan Laurie &lt;dlaurie@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="323501" owner_email="adurbin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/01/323501/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2015.07" change_id="I86c96a4092deab2dfa51b3043b9dba16b6a4c201" commit="8559310e080821024e238a40c46f94a398050963" commit_message="ec/google/chromeec: implement vboot_(save|retrieve)_hash API  For x86 systems which resume through the reset vector one needs to ensure the the RW slot taken at resume time matches the one at boot time. To that end, allow Chrome OS EC to supply the plumbing to vboot for storing and retrieving the RW slots' hash digest using the vstore backend.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:46049 BRANCH=glados TEST=Suspended and resumed on chell. Also, tested with an EC build      which returns a bad hash to ensure that is properly caught.  Change-Id: I86c96a4092deab2dfa51b3043b9dba16b6a4c201 Signed-off-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/323502 Reviewed-by: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Duncan Laurie &lt;dlaurie@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="323502" owner_email="adurbin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/02/323502/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2015.07" change_id="I40264019eb28e85795258112c720056a6a3fc523" commit="364105238417a6bcd16cc11e8d5b56d73f5426fe" commit_message="soc/intel/skylake: implement vboot_platform_is_resuming()  To allow skylake platforms to run with verified memory init code the chipset needs to implement vboot_platform_is_resuming() so that the vboot code can make proper decisions.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:46049 BRANCH=glados TEST=Suspended and resumed on chell. Also, tested with an EC build      which returns a bad hash to ensure that is properly caught.  Change-Id: I40264019eb28e85795258112c720056a6a3fc523 Signed-off-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/323503 Reviewed-by: Duncan Laurie &lt;dlaurie@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="323503" owner_email="adurbin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/03/323503/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2015.07" change_id="I5e467854bf065a138bd46e476a7e7088f51454ca" commit="f2044d6f8351230b28f94f4cfde2d494869c9632" commit_message="soc/intel/skylake: implement vboot_platform_prepare_reboot()  In order to not reboot loop in the face of failed vboot verification on resume set the PM1 control register to indicate S5. After the subsequent cold reset the PM1 control register will indicate S5 as it should.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:46049 BRANCH=glados TEST=On chell injected failed vboot verification. Ensured a reboot      loop doesn't ensue.  Change-Id: I5e467854bf065a138bd46e476a7e7088f51454ca Signed-off-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/323504 Reviewed-by: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Duncan Laurie &lt;dlaurie@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="323504" owner_email="adurbin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/04/323504/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2015.07" change_id="I8a5f2d154026ce794a70e7ec38883fa3c28fb6e7" commit="c8a6c4f5d08c107c11a5ff694ee8f0859041ec22" commit_message="vendorcode/google/chromeos: guard cbmem_find() in verstage and bootblock  When vboot_handoff_flag() is called in the bootblock or a separate verstage there's no memory nor the possibility of dram coming online. Therefore, don't bother to attempt call cbmem_find().  BUG=chrome-os-partner:44827 BRANCH=glados TEST=Built chell with separate verstage which pulls in vboot_common.c      dependency. No more linking errors w/ cbmem_find() not being      around.  Change-Id: I8a5f2d154026ce794a70e7ec38883fa3c28fb6e7 Signed-off-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/324070 Reviewed-by: Duncan Laurie &lt;dlaurie@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="324070" owner_email="adurbin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/70/324070/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2015.07" change_id="I2207819ec1490767cb1cf4b92e34e714783c1c22" commit="20f1bc0303b896afe30ca0f876a810b75926eac1" commit_message="lib: add bootmode.c to verstage  Some of the functions within bootmode.c may be required by boards in verstage. Therefore, allow this file to be built in verstage.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:44827 BRANCH=glados TEST=Built chell w/ bootmode.c dependencies in separate verstage.  Change-Id: I2207819ec1490767cb1cf4b92e34e714783c1c22 Signed-off-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/324071 Reviewed-by: Duncan Laurie &lt;dlaurie@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="324071" owner_email="adurbin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/71/324071/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2015.07" change_id="I95aeb97737d0ddfa6c53269c9d14db16ed5e47cc" commit="4d302cebec17e039a56bacb86fdc1be1041ad947" commit_message="mainboard/google/chell: perform early init for CAR *stage  In order to support both separate verstage and a verified boot after romstage one needs to ensure the proper GPIO and EC configuration been complete. Therefore, move that logic to car_mainboard_post_console_init() in car.c file which gets called in the early flow of a CAR stage (either verstage or romstage).  BUG=chrome-os-partner:44827 BRANCH=glados TEST=Built chell w/ separate verstage and booted.  Change-Id: I95aeb97737d0ddfa6c53269c9d14db16ed5e47cc Signed-off-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/324072 Reviewed-by: Duncan Laurie &lt;dlaurie@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="324072" owner_email="adurbin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/72/324072/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2015.07" change_id="Icc989ec5700b3f1a144a6b41198b7dd2c2aac6f7" commit="e2f6c29c66c5d0105a9dfe7bc36c5ac1ee1d382e" commit_message="mainboard/google/glados: perform early init for CAR *stage  In order to support both separate verstage and a verified boot after romstage one needs to ensure the proper GPIO and EC configuration been complete. Therefore, move that logic to car_mainboard_post_console_init() in car.c file which gets called in the early flow of a CAR stage (either verstage or romstage).  BUG=chrome-os-partner:44827 BRANCH=glados TEST=Built glados w/ separate verstage and booted.  Change-Id: Icc989ec5700b3f1a144a6b41198b7dd2c2aac6f7 Signed-off-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/324073 Reviewed-by: Duncan Laurie &lt;dlaurie@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="324073" owner_email="adurbin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/73/324073/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2015.07" change_id="I7281c4373fcbaaf0beedaa63dcf0dedb5316349f" commit="e94789d144b832f96f5012cd974845c8e251a114" commit_message="mainboard/intel/kunimitsu: perform early init for CAR *stage  In order to support both separate verstage and a verified boot after romstage one needs to ensure the proper GPIO and EC configuration been complete. Therefore, move that logic to car_mainboard_post_console_init() in car.c file which gets called in the early flow of a CAR stage (either verstage or romstage).  BUG=chrome-os-partner:44827 BRANCH=glados TEST=Built kunimitsu w/ separate verstage.  Change-Id: I7281c4373fcbaaf0beedaa63dcf0dedb5316349f Signed-off-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/324074 Reviewed-by: Duncan Laurie &lt;dlaurie@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="324074" owner_email="adurbin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/74/324074/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2015.07" change_id="I8d14ea16b2d07bbf04c